dist/
# The benchmark harness and ALL of its result artifacts are excluded from this
# repository and from its git history. Every sweep ran against ~/claude-plus-plus,
# a private third-party repository: the harness named files and symbols from that
# corpus, and the artifacts quoted its source. Nothing under bench/ is published.
#
# An earlier plan was to commit the artifacts with the verbatim report text stripped,
# so that the numbers in README.md would resolve to files a reader could open. That
# was reversed — stripping the report text was not enough, because the harness and
# the artifact metadata still identify the corpus. README.md states the exclusion
# and its consequence: the published numbers name the run and field they came from,
# and cannot be independently verified from this repository.
#
# This entry stays because untracked working copies may still exist on a developer's
# machine — including bench/results/raw-reports/, which holds the UNSTRIPPED reports
# and therefore ~1 MB of the private corpus's source. It is the last defence, not the
# first. Do not remove it, and do not force anything under it into a commit.
bench/
*.log
.claude-flow/
